# Prompt steering (topic · tool · inst)

Mirrored for Antigravity: [`.agents/rules/prompt-steering.md`](../../.agents/rules/prompt-steering.md)

Read before changing prompt behavior:

- [`_/docs/inst.md`](../../_/docs/inst.md) — inst rows, triggers, compose pipeline
- [`_/docs/site-ai.md`](../../_/docs/site-ai.md) — tool metadata, multi-site context
- [`_/schemas/topic.sql`](../../_/schemas/topic.sql) — topic seeds + persona chain

## Three layers

| Layer | Store | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| **Topic** | `ai.topic` | **Confine** — persona + tool eligibility |
| **Tool** | Rust `ToolDefinition` | **Capability** — what the model *can* call |
| **Inst** | `ai.inst` | **Steer** — how the model should behave this turn |

Inst tells the LLM *how*; tools tell it *what* it can call.

## Per-turn pipeline

```
ReqPrompt → topic_resolve → inst_pick → inst_block + tool_include/exclude → compose_tools_and_inst
```

Code: `servers/crates/mod_chat` — `compose/mod.rs`, `inst_macro.rs`, `prompt_turn.rs`.

## Topic (confine)

- Active topic: explicit `topic_id`, `@mention`, or default `general`.
- Tools gated by `topics`, `always`, `requires_kinds`, `requires_capability`.
- Topic persona: `ai.topic.inst` + `extend` chain — **not** merged into `ai.inst`.

## Inst (steer)

Kinds: `task` (phrases), `mention`, `topic`, `trigger` (`always`, `tool_include:`, `tool_exclude:`).

Pair inst body (what to do) with triggers (force/drop tools). Seeds: [`_/schemas/inst.sql`](../../_/schemas/inst.sql). Type B only — no new hardcoded steering in Rust.

## Wrong tool? Fix in order

1. **Topic** — should this tool be possible here? Adjust topic mapping or tool `topics`.
2. **Tool metadata** — registered? `readonly`, `requires_kinds`, `requires_capability`, `always`?
3. **Inst** — right tools available but model picks wrong? Add/refine inst + `tool_include` / `tool_exclude`.

Do not jump to inst when the tool was never eligible.

## Separate layers (do not merge)

| Store | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `ai.topic.inst` | Topic persona chain |
| `ai.inst` | Phrase/context steering |
| `identity.meta_json.inst_base` | Bot personality |

## File-specific inst work

When editing inst seeds or compose code, also follow `.cursor/rules/inst.mdc` / `.agents/rules/inst.md`.
